    {
      "id": "S4-05",
      "shot": "S4-05",
      "text": "That's only a picture. Real molecules don't spin like tiny propellers. They're jammed together, and they barely manage part of a turn before the field reverses. But the key idea holds. The field keeps shoving, and collisions scatter that shove into random jiggling. And random jiggling of molecules — that's what heat is.",
