      "shot": "S6-04",
      "text": "Frozen food has its own trick. Ice is bad at absorbing microwaves — its molecules are locked in place. But once one patch thaws into liquid water, it soaks up far more energy than the ice around it. So it heats faster, and faster still — which is how one bite can be scalding while the next is frozen solid.",
